oat to kojima as i  can not handle any spinning rides  luckily i can play fps games so i will  be able to enjoy death lube later a game  that our very own timur hussein gave a  10 out of 10. and if you want to know  why death loop is good enough to be  gamespot's 20th perfect score then make  sure you go check out his review right  after this video  but all right let's talk about some  console updates now first up is  playstation because starting tomorrow  after a two month long firmware test ps5  users will be able to expand their  console storage with an nvme m.2 ssd  instead of something proprietary like  microsoft's official expansion option  unless of course you're down for trying  the modded version that one xbox user  detailed in a blog post you can check  out yesterday's news video for more on  that tomorrow's playstation 5 system  update will also bring the console's 3d  audio tech from headsets to built-in tv  speakers meanwhile users of sony's pulse  3d wireless headset will receive access  to an equalizer as part of the update  some other quality of life changes  include the ability to customize the  control center by rearranging or hiding  certain buttons sending messages from  the game base and see more details at a  glance about your own games in the game  library for more info on this update  make sure to visit gamespot.com  and over on the microsoft side of things  windows pcs are getting an update to the  xbox app that introduces functionality  allowing users to stream console games  from their home console or the cloud  this functionality is live now for game  pass ultimate subscribers in 22  countries before this the xbox cloud  gaming service worked on phones tablets  and pcs through the browser but now it's  baked directly into the xbox app and as  for streaming games from your home  console microsoft says this is quote  essentially a way to mirror your console  gaming experience on another screen this  happens through the xbox remote play  feature inside the xbox app for windows  10 pcs  and now i want you to hit the comment  section and let me know your preferred  way to play is it streaming from the  cloud streaming from a console or just  directly on that console  see you later  [Music]  you
 

